# Web A11y & UX Conventions

## Modals

- All modals must have `role="dialog"`, `aria-modal="true"`, and `aria-labelledby` pointing to the heading
- Never use `window.confirm()` or `window.alert()` — use in-app modals
- Destructive actions (delete, revoke) must use a red-styled confirmation modal that explains consequences

```html
<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<div v-if="showModal" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="modal-title">
  <h3 id="modal-title">Confirm Delete</h3>
</div>
```

## Page States

- Every data-fetching page must handle all three states: loading (skeleton or spinner), error (message + retry), empty (illustration or next-step guidance)
- Show toast feedback after mutations (create, delete, update) via `useToast()`

## Forms

- Every `<input>` must have a `<label>` with matching `for`/`id`
- Use `sr-only` class for visually hidden labels when the UI context is obvious

## Toggle Switches

- Use `<button role="switch" :aria-checked="value">`, not `<div @click>`

## Tab Strips

- Container: `role="tablist"`
- Each tab: `role="tab"`, `:aria-selected="isActive"`

## Interactive Controls

- Buttons with only an icon must have `aria-label`
- Expandable menus/hamburgers must have `:aria-expanded`
- Never hide actions behind hover-only (`opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100`) without a mobile fallback — use `md:opacity-0 md:group-hover:opacity-100`

## Links

- All `NuxtLink` / `<a>` hrefs must resolve to real routes — no dead links
- 404 states should include a back-link to the parent list page

## Styling Consistency

- Use `text-gray-400` for secondary text — never mix in `text-slate-*` variants
- Use Tailwind v4 syntax: `!` suffix for importance (`border-gray-500/10!`), `bg-linear-to-r` not `bg-gradient-to-r`
